[32m+[m[32m# Planar Arm ROS 2 Controller[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mROS 2 Jazzy control, teleoperation, and RViz visualization for a 3-DoF planar[m
[32m+[m[32marm. The provided[m
[32m+[m[32m[`planar_arm.py`](src/planar_arm_control/planar_arm_control/planar_arm.py)[m
[32m+[m[32mkinematics library is used unchanged.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Arm conventions[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe planner's coordinates are planar `(x, y)` with `y >= 0` as the ground[m
[32m+[m[32mconstraint. The URDF uses ROS's Z-up convention, so planner `y` maps to robot[m
[32m+[m[32m`z`; all three revolute joints rotate around the negative Y axis. `base_link`[m
[32m+[m[32mis located at the shoulder; Gazebo spawns it 0.2 m above the floor. Link[m
[32m+[m[32mlengths are `[3.0, 2.0, 1.5]`, in meters. Joint limits are:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Joint | Lower | Upper |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---:|---:|[m
[32m+[m[32m| joint1 | 0° | 180° |[m
[32m+[m[32m| joint2 | -120° | 120° |[m
[32m+[m[32m| joint3 | -120° | 120° |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Build[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInstall ROS 2 Jazzy and the controller/visualization dependencies:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32msudo apt install \[m
[32m+[m[32m  ros-jazzy-ros2-control ros-jazzy-ros2-controllers \[m
[32m+[m[32m  ros-jazzy-robot-state-publisher ros-jazzy-xacro ros-jazzy-rviz2 \[m
[32m+[m[32m  ros-jazzy-joy python3-numpy python3-pyqt5 python3-pyqtgraph[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFrom the workspace root:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32msource /opt/ros/jazzy/setup.bash[m
[32m+[m[32mcolcon build[m
[32m+[m[32msource install/setup.bash[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Launch[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mStandalone controller plus teleoperation GUI (in-process simulated arm):[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mros2 launch planar_arm_control bringup.launch.py[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRobot description, state publisher, and RViz with the simulated controller:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mros2 launch planar_arm_control display.launch.py[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe gamepad listener subscribes to `/joy`; start a joystick driver separately[m
[32m+[m[32mwith `ros2 run joy joy_node`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Command and telemetry interfaces[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* `/target_pose` (`geometry_msgs/PointStamped`): planar target with `point.x`[m
[32m+[m[32m  as robot X and `point.z` as planner Y/robot Z, relative to `base_link`.[m
[32m+[m[32m  `point.y` is ignored. Targets outside the arm's maximum reach, targets[m
[32m+[m[32m  without a valid IK solution, and paths that violate joint or ground[m
[32m+[m[32m  constraints are rejected and reported on `/controller_status`.[m
[32m+[m[32m* `/joint_target` (`std_msgs/Float64MultiArray`): three joint positions in[m
[32m+[m[32m  radians. This shares the same path planner and constraint checks.[m
[32m+[m[32m* `/joint_states` (`sensor_msgs/JointState`): fixed-rate state in standalone[m
[32m+[m[32m  mode. The `ros2_control` backend accepts feedback from a configured[m
[32m+[m[32m  joint-state source.[m
[32m+[m[32m* `/joint_trajectory_controller/joint_trajectory`[m
[32m+[m[32m  (`trajectory_msgs/JointTrajectory`): optional ros2_control backend command[m
[32m+[m[32m  stream.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mExample Cartesian command:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mros2 topic pub --once /target_pose geometry_msgs/msg/PointStamped \[m
[32m+[m[32m  "{header: {frame_id: base_link}, point: {x: 4.0, y: 0.0, z: 2.0}}"[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe controller uses a quintic time scaling with zero endpoint velocity and[m
[32m+[m[32macceleration. `publish_rate_hz`, `trajectory_duration`,[m
[32m+[m[32m`max_joint_velocity`, `backend_mode`, topic names, joystick rates/steps, and[m
[32m+[m[32mthe joystick trajectory duration are ROS parameters. `backend_mode` is[m
[32m+[m[32m`simulated` for standalone runs and `ros2_control` for use with a configured[m
[32m+[m[32mcontroller. The repository includes Gazebo model assets, but no Gazebo launch[m
[32m+[m[32mfile. The planner depends on the small[m
[32m+[m[32m`JointCommandBackend` boundary; a hardware adapter can replace the backend[m
[32m+[m[32mwithout changing IK, trajectory timing, or constraint validation.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Teleoperation[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m* GUI Cartesian fields send planner XY targets (robot X/Z); joint fields send a[m
[32m+[m[32m  joint-space target.[m
[32m+[m[32m  The live plot shows the arm, end-effector coordinates, and joint angles.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Keyboard controls (when the GUI window has focus): `W/A/S/D` or arrow keys[m
[32m+[m[32m  jog the end effector in XY; `1/2`, `3/4`, and `5/6` jog joints 1, 2, and 3[m
[32m+[m[32m  down/up.[m
[32m+[m[32m* Gamepad: axes 0/1 jog XY (Y is inverted by default for common sticks);[m
[32m+[m[32m  rising button pairs `0/1`, `2/3`, and `4/5` jog joints 1, 2, and 3 down/up.[m
[32m+[m[32m  Axis sign/speed and joint jog step are parameters.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll jogs are converted into targets and pass through the same IK/trajectory[m
[32m+[m[32mplanner and safety checks.[m
